class.description:
A [LocalizationCatalogList] names the catalog files of a project, a DLC or a mod, each with a priority. The file name of a path may contain the wildcards [code]*[/code] and [code]?[/code] (for example [code]exec://mods/*.lcat[/code]); [method get_catalog_paths] expands them and sorts all paths by priority. When two catalogs have the same key, the later one (higher priority) wins.
Entries are edited in the inspector as an array (path and priority) or with the methods below.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var list = LocalizationCatalogList.new()
list.add_entry("res://translations/game.lcat")
list.add_entry("exec://mods/*.json", 10)
for path in list.get_catalog_paths():
	var catalog = TextLocalizationCatalog.new()
	catalog.load_from_file(path)
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
var list = new LocalizationCatalogList();
list.AddEntry("res://translations/game.lcat");
list.AddEntry("exec://mods/*.json", 10);
foreach (string path in list.GetCatalogPaths())
{
	var catalog = new TextLocalizationCatalog();
	catalog.LoadFromFile(path);
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
